# Hush mobile — environment variables.
# Copy to `.env` for local dev (Expo auto-loads it). For EAS builds these are
# set per-profile under `build.<profile>.env` in eas.json, or as EAS secrets.
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_*-prefixed vars are embedded in the client bundle.

# Base URL of the Hush API (e.g. https://api.hush.app).
# Empty / unset => the app stays on the local fixture model and remains
# unenrolled (no telemetry sink). This is the intended default until the
# backend is reachable and an invite token is issued.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# ── THE COACH ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Cloudflare Worker that holds the Gemini key. The app talks only to this; the
# key itself lives in Cloudflare's secret store and is never in a build, a file, or
# this repo (`noKeyEverReachesTheRepo` fails the build if one ever lands here).
#
# Both of these are EXPO_PUBLIC_*, which means both are EMBEDDED IN THE BUNDLE.
# The URL is not a secret. The token is a speed bump that stops the scanners which
# find every new *.workers.dev hostname within days — anyone who unpacks the app
# can read it, and that is a property of shipping a client, not an oversight.
#
# Unset => the app never calls the coach at all (`coachIsReachable()` is false).
EXPO_PUBLIC_COACH_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_COACH_TOKEN=
